        "description": "<p>Recently <a href=\"https://x.com/Merocle/status/2015496917472489751\">this post from @Merocle</a> caught my eye:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm fixing my iFixit soldering station. I haven't used it for a long time and the battery has gone overdischarge. I hope it will come back to life. Unfortunately, there are no replacements available for sale at the moment.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<figure class=\"insert-image\"><img src=\"https://www.jeffgeerling.com/blog/2026/ode-to-the-aa-battery/ifixit-soldering-usb-battery-merocle-torn-down.jpg\"\n alt=\"iFixit soldering hub torn down - used with permission\" width=\"500\" height=\"auto\">\n</figure>\n\n<p>Devices with built-in rechargeable batteries have been bugging me a lot lately. It's convenient to have a device you can take with you and use anywhere. And with modern Li-ion cells, battery life is remarkable.</p>",
